in the past three weeks more than 70  people have been killed in mass  shootings  the most recent at a medical center in  tulsa oklahoma  where four people were murdered by a man  said to be a disgruntled patient police  say the gunman then killed himself he  bought one of his guns just a few hours  before we know  through the help of our atf  and their gun tracing that at 2 pm  on june the first  mr lewis purchased  a semi-automatic rifle  from a local gun store  the same weapon was used to kill 19  children and two teachers at a texas  elementary school last week  the same weapon used to murder 10 people  at a grocery store in buffalo new york  10 days before that  in both cases the alleged gunman were  just 18 years old the texas shooter  killed at the scene the buffalo shooting  suspect was arraigned on murder charges  thursday  in a rare prime time address to the  american people president biden urged  congress to impose federal gun controls  suggesting a ban on automatic weapons  and high capacity magazines  raising the age at which an individual  can buy a gun from 18 to 21  and removing the protections against  litigation enjoyed by gun manufacturers  they had one message for all of us  do something  just do something  for god's sake do something some of  these measures suggested by president  biden are already being debated and may  well be passed in the  democrat-controlled house of  representatives  but they're likely to be blocked by  senate republicans who were a particular  target of president biden's anger but my  god  the fact that the majority of the senate  republicans  don't want any of these proposals even  to be debated  or come up for a vote  i find unconscionable  we can't fail the american people again  a message too for the american people  that the majority should act and turn  their outrage into making the issue  central to their vote  mike hannah al-jazeera washington
 

